<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>It is completed normally, save that all images of Prince Adam from Beauty and the Beast have been colored over and scratched out using the red crayon.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No sentence has ever made me feel dread faster than this. Ever. There is a very distinct death of innocence in this line: there is no Prince Charming to save her - or if she had one, that he ruined her in a way that fairy tales don't matter anymore. There is no coping when your coping mechanism has been shattered before your eyes.</p>
<p>You can't escape with the dog - what was once soft is crusted to the point where you've lost something comforting. You can't escape with the game - there's no true contact to be made with the lack of speech.</p>
<p>There's just nothing.</p>
